# Knowledge Lifecycle System

Spec: Lifecycle
Purpose:
   Define the knowledge lifecycle system that prevents .sdd from
   becoming a knowledge dump. Knowledge nodes transition through
   states (Candidate → Active → Stale → Deprecated → Superseded →
   Archived) and are periodically evaluated by the garbage collector
   and compactor. Introduces the claim/challenge system, confidence
   scoring, health monitoring, compaction, drift detection, and
   the learning loop pipeline.

Owns: lifecycle/

## Lifecycle States

  CANDIDATE     — identified as potentially reusable but not yet validated
  ACTIVE        — currently referenced by tasks/decisions (last 7 days)
  STALE         — not referenced recently but not yet superseded
  DEPRECATED    — superseded by newer knowledge (@supersedes relationship)
  SUPERSEDED    — explicitly replaced by newer knowledge
  DELETE_BLOCKED— deletion blocked by active dependencies
  ARCHIVED      — preserved for historical reference only

## Quality Dimensions

  DUPLICATE        — identical or near-identical content to another node
  FRAGMENTED       — should be merged with related nodes
  ORPHAN           — no incoming @references from other nodes
  UNUSED           — not referenced for N+ days (configurable)
  CONTRADICTED     — conflicts with higher-trust knowledge
  SUPERSEDED       — replaced by newer knowledge
  TERMINOLOGY_DRIFT — codebase terms diverge from policy terms
  ARCHITECTURE_DRIFT — code violates declared architecture

## Knowledge Promotion Levels (L0-L4)

  L0 — Observation (@observation.*): seen once in a single context
  L1 — Discovery (@discovery.*): repeated pattern, potentially reusable
  L2 — Candidate (@candidate.*): reusable knowledge candidate
  L3 — Validated Knowledge (@skill.* / @concept.*): confirmed by evidence
  L4 — Project Rule (@policy.* / @decision.*): project-wide norm with authority

  See: @learning-loop.sdd for full promotion pipeline and rules.

## Claim System

  Claims (@claim.*) are assertable statements backed by evidence.
  Claim lifecycle: PROPOSED → SUPPORTED → VALIDATED → ACTIVE →
  CHALLENGED → INVALIDATED / SUPERSEDED.

  Challenges (@challenge.*) contest claims with counter-evidence.

  See: @claims.sdd and @challenges.sdd for full specification.

## Confidence & Decay

  Confidence: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH with numeric scores (0.0–1.0).
  Confidence promotes with evidence, tests, usage, and human validation.
  Confidence demotes with failures, contradictions, and changes.

  Knowledge decay factors: age (signal, not verdict), usage frequency,
  failure rate, dependency changes, technology changes, contradicting evidence.

  See: @confidence.sdd for full specification.

## Health Score

  Per-node health score (0-100) based on usage, evidence, failures, age,
  and conflicts. Health is distinct from status — a node can be ACTIVE
  with low health, signaling it needs review.

  See: @health-score.sdd for formula and graph health reports.

## Safe Garbage Collection Protocol

  DISCOVER → REPORT → PROPOSE → APPROVE → APPLY
  Never auto-delete — only propose ARCHIVE, MERGE, or DEPRECATE.

  Dependency check: delete attempt on entity with active dependencies
  → DELETE_BLOCKED state.

  Trust-aware pruning by data classification:
    SECRET → minimal retention, encrypted archive
    RESTRICTED → never pruned
    CONFIDENTIAL → 365-day retention
    INTERNAL → 180-day retention
    PUBLIC → 90-day retention

  See: @gc-policy.sdd for full specification.

## Knowledge Compactor

  Compactor combines fragmented knowledge into canonical concepts.
  Distinct from GC (which removes waste). Compactor protocol:
  DISCOVERIES → CLUSTER → COMMON PATTERN → CONCEPT → EVIDENCE LINKS.

  Core + Variant specialization: @skill.retry (core) → @skill.payment-retry (variant).
  Specialization via explicit `specializes:` edge, not deep extends chains.

  See: @compactor.sdd for full specification.

## Generation Tracking

  Each knowledge entity carries a generation number that increments
  on revision, challenge acceptance, or promotion. Provides full
  lineage tracing: observation → discovery → candidate → skill.

  See: @generation.sdd for full specification.

## Drift Detection

  Terminology drift: codebase terms diverge from policy/concept terms.
  Architecture drift: code violates declared architecture boundaries.
  Violations have lifecycle: DETECTED → REVIEWED → ACCEPTED/FALSE_POSITIVE → FIXED → VERIFIED.
  Architecture exceptions (@exception.*) are time-limited with expiry dates.

  See: @drift.sdd for full specification.

## Learning Loop

  Full pipeline: OBSERVATION → DISCOVERY → CANDIDATE → EVIDENCE → CLAIM →
  VALIDATION → KNOWLEDGE. Bidirectional — knowledge can be downgraded
  via challenge or contradiction.

  Learning boundary: AI can observe/discover/propose but CANNOT promote
  to L3 or L4 without human approval.

  See: @learning-loop.sdd for full specification.

## Agents

   @agent.knowledge-cleaner — runs garbage collection proposals
   @agent.knowledge-compactor — runs compaction (merge duplicates)

   Both operate at AUTONOMY L1 (Suggest) — they PROPOSE, human/AI approves.

## Garbage Collector Protocol

  SCANNING: enumerate all .sdd nodes
  ANALYZING: check each node against quality dimensions
  SCORING: calculate quality score per node
  PROPOSING: generate @proposal.knowledge-cleanup for review
  WAITING: human/AI reviews and approves/denies
  EXECUTING: approved proposals update node state

  NEVER delete — only propose ARCHIVE or MERGE.

## Compaction Protocol

  1. FIND_DUPLICATES: detect nodes with identical/similar content
  2. MERGE: combine fragments into canonical version
  3. UPDATE_REFERENCES: redirect all @references to canonical
  4. ARCHIVE_ORIGINAL: mark merged nodes as ARCHIVED with @supercedes
  5. AUDIT: record compaction in execution journal

## Trust-Aware Pruning

  Classification      →  Retention Policy
  ──────────────────────────────────────────
  SECRET             →  Minimal retention, encrypted archive
  RESTRICTED         →  Never pruned
  CONFIDENTIAL       →  365-day retention before archive
  INTERNAL           →  180-day retention, aggressive compaction
  PUBLIC             →  90-day retention, aggressive compaction

## Lifecycle Trigger

  .sdd-bootstrap
    ↓ 5. Context Compiler loads lifecycle policy
    ...
    During execution:
    ↓
    After task completion:
    AI runs @agent.knowledge-cleaner
    AI runs @agent.knowledge-compactor

